Question 3: Where are the credentials stored? and what are the options other than --global? Should the credentials be pushed to github? 

Using a local folder as the DVC remote, by using the following commands:
mkdir ../dvc_local_remote
dvc remote add -d local_remote "C:\Users\User\Documents\dvc_local_remote"
git add .dvc/config
git commit -m "Configure local folder as dvc remote"
git push

Credentials location depends on scope:
--global : stored in OS-level global DVC config
--local : stored in .dvc/config.local inside the repo
No flag (project-level or default) : stored in .dvc/config, which is committed to git.
The other scope options besides --global are: --local and --system, plus the default project-level scope.
No, credentials should never be pushed to GitHub.
	
