Question 4: Take a look at the .gitignore file. Explain what happened.

DVC appends data/ (or the specific tracked path) to .gitignore. This happens because once a folder is tracked by dvc add, git must stop tracking the actual files (they're big binary data) and instead only track the small pointer file DVC creates. The .gitignore entry is what prevents git from accidentally picking the raw data back up.
-------------------------------------------------------------
Question 5: Do you see a .dvc file? What does it contain? 

Yes, data.dvc. It's a small text file containing:
the outs path (data)
an md5 hash of the folder's contents
the size: This pointer is what git actually versions. DVC uses the hash to know exactly which version of the data folder to fetch from the remote on dvc checkout/dvc pull.
